    <qti-feedback-block identifier="CORRECT" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Correct! Something fathomable can be understood or figured out, even if it takes real effort.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="INCORRECT" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Something fathomable can be understood or figured out, even if it takes real effort. Remember the parts: fathom + able. The other sentences misuse fathomable — wrong strength, wrong situation, or wrong pairing. The correct one is: &quot;The physicist&apos;s equations were dense, but after a semester of study, they became fathomable.&quot;</p></qti-content-body>
